cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use trainnr, please cite the software; if you build on its
  results, please cite the paper under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: "trainnr: the end-to-end robotics platform, from real-to-sim through training to a gated deployment"
abstract: >-
  The end-to-end robotics platform, run from a coding agent: a robot's
  dynamics are identified from its own telemetry into a content-hashed
  simulation model, training datasets are generated with recorded
  provenance, policies are trained by reinforcement learning (MuJoCo,
  mjlab) or imitation learning (LeRobot) on the identified model with a
  measured randomization span, evaluated with paired trials and exact
  intervals, gated against the robot's runtime, deployed, and watched
  through their telemetry for drift, which starts the next turn. One MCP
  server, the Studio (a desktop app) and a Claude Code plugin.
